      {
        "exercise": 1,
        "pages": "123",
        "task": "Turn the letters into words, then transcribe them",
        "method": "Join the letters and apply the combinations: hamzah + alif = آ, laam + alif = لَا. If the word starts with alif + laam it is the article: laam with sukuun = moon (say ʔal); no sukuun and a shaddah next = sun.",
        "example": {
          "ar": "اَلْآخِرَةُ",
          "translit": "ʔal ʔaa khi ra tu",
          "note": "#3 · hamzah + alif = آ; moon laam"
        },
        "contrast": {
          "ar": "اَللَّيْلُ",
          "translit": "ʔal lay lu",
          "note": "#11 · sun laam on ل itself: shaddah on the next ل"
        }
      },
